{"story_id":"GL-28932-001","title":"The two Friends who set off to travel round the world","title_raw":"The two Friends who set off to travel round the world","notes":"","language":"en","original_language":"kl","country":"Greenland","country_code":"GL","culture_region":"グリーンランド(イヌイット)","latitude":64.0,"longitude":-45.0,"location_precision":"culture_region","map_location_type":"source_culture_region","collector":"Knud Rasmussen","translator":"W. J. Alexander Worster","publication_year":1921,"year_evidence":"扉に 1921","book_id":"PG-28932","book_title":"Eskimo Folk-Tales","source_provider":"Project Gutenberg","source_url":"https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/28932","source_title":"Eskimo Folk-Tales","license_status":"PUBLIC_DOMAIN_US","license_name":"Public Domain (United States)","license_jurisdiction":"US","rights_evidence_url":"https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/28932","redistribution_allowed":true,"commercial_use":true,"derivative_use":true,"ml_processing_status":"reviewed","verification_date":"2026-09-08","word_count":262,"text":"Once there were two men who desired to travel round the world, that\nthey might tell others what was the manner of it.\n\nThis was in the days when men were still many on the earth, and there\nwere people in all the lands. Now we grow fewer and fewer. Evil and\nsickness have come upon men. See how I, who tell this story, drag my\nlife along, unable to stand upon my feet.\n\nThe two men who were setting out had each newly taken a wife, and had\nas yet no children. They made themselves cups of musk-ox horn, each\nmaking a cup for himself from one side of the same beast's head. And\nthey set out, each going away from the other, that they might go by\ndifferent ways and meet again some day. They travelled with sledges,\nand chose land to stay and live upon each summer.\n\nIt took them a long time to get round the world; they had children,\nand they grew old, and then their children also grew old, until\nat last the parents were so old that they could not walk, but the\nchildren led them.\n\nAnd at last one day, they met--and of their drinking horns there was\nbut the handle left, so many times had they drunk water by the way,\nscraping the horn against the ground as they filled them.\n\n\"The world is great indeed,\" they said when they met.\n\nThey had been young at their starting, and now they were old men,\nled by their children.\n\nTruly the world is great.","cluster":3,"analysis":{"analysis_version":"1.0","embedding_model":"intfloat/multilingual-e5-small","themes":[{"label":"旅","z":0.884,"strength":"中","confidence":0.708,"method":"embedding"}],"motifs":[],"animals":[{"label":"牛","count":1,"method":"count","confidence":1.0}],"nature":[{"label":"海","count":1,"method":"count","confidence":1.0}],"events":[{"position":0.0,"label":null,"hits":0,"lift":0.0,"method":"count"},{"position":0.091,"label":null,"hits":0,"lift":0.0,"method":"count"},{"position":0.182,"label":null,"hits":0,"lift":0.0,"method":"count"},{"position":0.273,"label":null,"hits":0,"lift":0.0,"method":"count"},{"position":0.364,"label":null,"hits":0,"lift":0.0,"method":"count"},{"position":0.455,"label":"Departure","hits":1,"lift":142.35,"method":"count"},{"position":0.545,"label":"Journey","hits":1,"lift":76.71,"method":"count"},{"position":0.636,"label":null,"hits":0,"lift":0.0,"method":"count"},{"position":0.727,"label":null,"hits":0,"lift":0.0,"method":"count"},{"position":0.818,"label":"Encounter","hits":1,"lift":42.87,"method":"count"},{"position":0.909,"label":null,"hits":0,"lift":0.0,"method":"count"},{"position":1.0,"label":"Encounter","hits":1,"lift":29.04,"method":"count"}],"tension":[{"position":0.0,"tension":1.0,"raw":0.0,"method":"lexicon"},{"position":0.091,"tension":0.0,"raw":-4.762,"method":"lexicon"},{"position":0.182,"tension":1.0,"raw":0.0,"method":"lexicon"},{"position":0.273,"tension":1.0,"raw":0.0,"method":"lexicon"},{"position":0.364,"tension":1.0,"raw":0.0,"method":"lexicon"},{"position":0.455,"tension":1.0,"raw":0.0,"m